{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in today because of some weight gain and lab changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve gained about 5 pounds in the last couple of days. I didn’t change my diet or anything. My regular labs showed my creatinine was up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We just got your ultrasound results. There’s swelling in the kidney from your transplant — it’s called hydronephrosis. That’s likely why your creatinine is rising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is that serious? The kidney’s not draining?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The ureter — the tube from the kidney to the bladder — seems blocked, probably from inflammation or swelling. We’ll need to place a temporary tube to drain the kidney."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A tube? Will that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s called a percutaneous nephrostomy. You’ll get light sedation, and it’s done with ultrasound guidance. It’s very safe and will help protect your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. When will it happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-12-13 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today. The interventional radiology team is ready. After that, we’ll monitor your labs and see how the kidney responds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The procedure went smoothly. The nephrostomy tube is in place and draining urine well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean the blockage is fixed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not completely. They tried to thread the tube all the way into the bladder, but there was too much swelling. So for now, it’s draining externally into a bag."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so I’ll have this bag for a while?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just temporarily. In a few days, they’ll try again to advance it into the bladder. For now, the important thing is that your kidney is draining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about the infection I was on antibiotics for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-12-13 19:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were on cefpodoxime for a suspected UTI. We sent a urine sample from the nephrostomy tube to check for infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine culture came back. It grew VRE — that’s a type of resistant enterococcus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "VRE? I’ve heard that’s tough to treat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but we have an effective antibiotic — linezolid. It works well against VRE and can be taken by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I stop the cefpodoxime?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re stopping it. It won’t work against VRE. You’ll start linezolid twice a day for 10 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-12-14 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-12-14 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine was 2.7 when you came in. This morning it’s 2.4 — that’s a good sign the drainage is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-12-14 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Does that mean the kidney is recovering?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-12-14 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a positive trend. We’ll keep monitoring it. You’re also passing small amounts of urine on your own, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-12-15 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, your labs are stable today. Creatinine is still 2.4. The nephrostomy tube is draining well, and you’re feeling okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-12-15 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no pain, I’m eating and walking. But I’m worried about being on Coumadin. Is it safe with the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-12-15 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good question. We’re holding your Coumadin for now. The tube site could bleed, so we’ll restart it only after the next procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-12-15 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. When will they try to move the tube into the bladder?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-12-15 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be scheduled for a nephrogram in the next few days — they’ll inject contrast to see the ureter and try to advance the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-12-15 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat urine culture today showed no growth. That means the linezolid is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-12-15 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful news. So the infection is clearing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-12-15 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and you’ll finish the full 10-day course at home to make sure it stays gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well — stable labs, eating, moving around. We’d like to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the linezolid twice daily for 10 days. Keep the nephrostomy bag empty and watch for fever, pain, or decreased output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most are the same. We’re adding furosemide to help with fluid balance and adjusting your metoprolol and levothyroxine doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still hold it. The transplant team will tell you when to restart after the next procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow up with them. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if you have fevers, chills, chest pain, or any drop in urine output — from either the tube or your own voiding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m glad we caught this early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So are we. The tube helped prevent further kidney damage. You’re going home in good shape."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-12-16 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check — you’re alert, no pain, vitals stable. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-12-16 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-12-16 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing — should I watch for any side effects from linezolid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. It can cause nausea or headache. Rarely, it affects blood counts or nerves with long use. But 10 days is safe for most people."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch for that and call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re very attentive — that helps a lot with recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I shower with the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but keep the site dry. Use a waterproof cover or plastic wrap. Don’t submerge it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And how often should I empty the bag?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Every 4 to 6 hours, or when it’s half full. Make sure it’s below your kidney level when you’re sitting or lying down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks again for all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-12-16 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. You handled this really well. Take care at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-12-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just confirming — I’ll get a call about the nephrogram appointment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-12-16 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, interventional radiology will contact you within the next few days to schedule it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-12-16 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m ready to go home now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-12-13 16:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-12-16 13:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a 5-pound weight gain and rising creatinine from her baseline, prompting evaluation that revealed hydronephrosis in her transplanted kidney. A percutaneous nephrostomy tube was placed on admission to relieve the obstruction, though it could not be advanced into the bladder due to inflammation. Her creatinine initially remained elevated at 2.7 but improved to 2.4 by discharge. Urine cultures from the nephrostomy tube identified VRE, leading to a switch from cefpodoxime to oral linezolid for a 10-day course. She remained stable, afebrile, and without pain, with ongoing urine output through both the tube and spontaneous voiding. She was discharged home with instructions to continue linezolid, monitor nephrostomy output, hold Coumadin, and follow up for a nephrogram to advance the tube. No growth was seen on repeat urine culture, indicating treatment response.",
    "problems": [
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Other ureteric obstruction",
      "Hydronephrosis",
      "Streptococcus infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site, streptococcus, group D [Enterococcus]",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Primary hyperparathyroidism",
      "Mitral valve disorders",
      "Tricuspid valve disorders, specified as nonrheumatic",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation"
    ]
  }
}
